Package: ringzero-security
Version: 0.1.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1
Recommends: bpftool, linux-tools-generic, curl
Maintainer: Ring Zero Security <abhijit@ringzerosecurity.com>
Homepage: https://ringzerosecurity.com
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/ringzerosec/jev-agentic-security
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/ringzerosec/jev-agentic-security
Description: Ring Zero Security — kernel-level runtime security for AI coding agents
 Ring Zero Security monitors and controls AI coding agent behavior at the OS
 level. See what your AI tools access, block what they shouldn't. Enforcement
 happens in the kernel via eBPF LSM hooks, underneath the agent process.
 .
 Features: credential access monitoring, sensitive file blocking,
 DLP (data loss prevention), heuristic prompt injection detection,
 TLS plaintext capture via eBPF uprobes, real-time event timeline,
 intent-action causal tracing, session management, webhooks for external
 detection systems, and the rz CLI.
 .
 The optional desktop viewer is a separate package, ringzero-desktop, so a
 server does not pull in the GTK/WebKit stack.
 .
 Supported agents: Claude Code, ChatGPT, Gemini, Cursor, Copilot,
 Codex, Devin, Windsurf, and any custom process you configure.
 .
 Kernel requirements: Linux 5.8+ with CONFIG_BPF_LSM=y and
 CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF=y. The installer configures GRUB automatically.
